    guide: [{ heading: "What the contrast checker verifies", body: "Check WCAG 2.1 contrast ratio between foreground and background colors instantly offline with AA and AAA badges for normal and large text. Enter charcoal #1a1a1a on white #ffffff to see 12.6 to 1 passing AAA, or medium #767676 on white for 4.54 to 1 passing AA. Designers audit body copy, buttons, placeholders and chart labels for accessibility before shipping. Example 1: white #ffffff on navy #1e3a5f scores above 12 to 1 and suits hero banners. Example 2: coral #ff5733 on white stalls near 3 to 1, failing paragraphs but surviving oversized headlines. Luminance math executes locally with live ratio and badge updates, never uploading palettes. Support teams auditing dashboards test slate #334155 on mist #f8fafc and white on navy #1e3a5f across desktop and mobile widths, logging ratios in accessibility statements that satisfy procurement reviewers and enterprise clients requiring AA compliance." }, { heading: "How AA and AAA thresholds work", body: "Contrast divides lighter and darker luminance offsets, yielding scores from 1 to 1 up to 21 to 1 for black on white. Table — Pair | Ratio | Verdict: #1a1a1a on #ffffff | 12.6 to 1 | AAA pass; #767676 on #ffffff | 4.54 to 1 | AA pass; #595959 on #ffffff | 7.0 to 1 | AAA pass; #999999 on #ffffff | 2.85 to 1 | fail; #ff5733 on #ffffff | 3.0 to 1 | large-only. Normal copy needs 4.5 to 1 for AA and 7 to 1 for AAA, while large 18pt text needs 3 to 1 and 4.5 to 1 respectively. Darken failing grays from #999999 to #595959 to cross AA without hue shifts, testing both sizes locally. Table captions, placeholder hints and disabled buttons often fail first because thin strokes and low opacity dilute effective luminance dramatically under office glare, so designers darken these elements two steps beyond body copy minimums for safety." }, { heading: "Contrast fixes, edges and related tools", body: "Adjust lightness before hue when repairing failures, preserving brand recognition while climbing ratios efficiently. Edge case: thin 12px light gray #9ca3af placeholders inside pale #f8fafc inputs can score below 2 to 1 despite looking stylish, blocking low-vision users entirely. Limitation: color math only, without font weight, layout, focus indicator or transparency blending checks, so manual keyboard review remains mandatory. For HEX to RGB translation of approved pairs, copy values using our tool at /color-converter. For harmonious alternatives that retain contrast, explore palettes at /color-palette, free offline with nothing uploaded. Marketing pages pairing coral #ff5733 headlines with charcoal #1a1a1a buttons preserve brand energy while passing audits, documenting approved combinations in Figma libraries that prevent regressions when new contributors join campaign sprints." }],
